From: arttttt <artem-bambalov@yandex.ru>
Subject: [PATCH] surfaceflinger: back-pressure can be switched off again

Android 11 and earlier read debug.sf.disable_backpressure. Android 12
removed the switch: a frame whose previous present fence has not fired
within the 1 ms grace is always skipped when that frame was composed by
the device. Only client composition still has a switch of its own.

On mocha the composer draws part of the frame on the GPU itself (the
Vulkan executor). SurfaceFlinger counts that as device composition, so
when the composer's drawing finishes after vblank the flip slips one
refresh, the present fence is late, and SurfaceFlinger then drops its
own next frame as well. One late drawing costs two frames. In the
recents trace v41 that happened 71 times.

The switch is back, read once at start as before. It defaults to off,
which leaves the Android 12 behaviour unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
index f2d8eb2..4179462 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
@@ -473,6 +473,15 @@ SurfaceFlinger::SurfaceFlinger(Factory& factory) : SurfaceFlinger(factory, SkipI
     ALOGI_IF(mPropagateBackpressureClientComposition,
              "Enabling backpressure propagation for Client Composition");
 
+    // Android 11 and earlier let a device turn back-pressure off; 12 dropped
+    // the switch and kept only the client-composition one. Brought back for
+    // a device whose composer draws part of the frame itself: there a late
+    // present fence means the composer's own drawing ran long, and skipping
+    // the next frame on top of it makes one late frame cost two.
+    property_get("debug.sf.disable_backpressure", value, "0");
+    mPropagateBackpressure = !atoi(value);
+    ALOGI_IF(!mPropagateBackpressure, "Disabling backpressure propagation");
+
     property_get("ro.surface_flinger.supports_background_blur", value, "0");
     bool supportsBlurs = atoi(value);
     mSupportsBlur = supportsBlurs;
@@ -1971,7 +1980,8 @@ void SurfaceFlinger::onMessageInvalidate(int64_t vsyncId, nsecs_t expectedVSyncT
     }
 
     if (framePending) {
-        if ((hwcFrameMissed && !gpuFrameMissed) || mPropagateBackpressureClientComposition) {
+        if (mPropagateBackpressure &&
+            ((hwcFrameMissed && !gpuFrameMissed) || mPropagateBackpressureClientComposition)) {
             signalLayerUpdate();
             return;
         }
diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.h b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.h
index a72dffe..5284564 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.h
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.h
@@ -1327,6 +1327,7 @@ private:
     bool mLayerCachingEnabled = false;
     volatile nsecs_t mDebugInTransaction = 0;
     bool mForceFullDamage = false;
+    bool mPropagateBackpressure = true;
     bool mPropagateBackpressureClientComposition = false;
     sp<SurfaceInterceptor> mInterceptor;
 
